{:ruleset :compustat
 :statement :income
 :taxonomy "us-gaap"
 :version "2026-07-28"
 :notes "Reclassification rules approximating Compustat income statement item
definitions (roadmap 4.1c). Derived empirically against a 2016-vintage WRDS
FUNDA extract (18 large industrials, FY2010-2015, ~120 firm-years): match
rates within 1% are quoted per rule as as-reported -> reclassified. Original
line items are always preserved alongside the reclassified ones. Residual
gaps are footnote-level allocations Compustat keys from disclosures absent in
the companyfacts API (e.g. partial D&A splits between COGS and SG&A, R&D
embedded in COGS, INDL-format restatements of firms with finance arms)."
 :aux {:cash-flow ["D&A"]}
 :rules
 [{:id :dp
   :target "DP (Compustat)"
   :compustat "DP"
   :formula [:= "D&A"]
   :notes "Depreciation and amortization. Compustat sources DP from the cash-flow
statement; the D&A operand is the cash-flow statement's (possibly derived)
line item. 65% within 1%; remaining gaps are DP definitional scope."}
  {:id :cogs-ex-da
   :target "COGS (Compustat)"
   :compustat "COGS"
   :formula [:- "Cost of Revenue" "D&A"]
   :guards [[:lt "D&A" "Cost of Revenue"]]
   :notes "Compustat COGS excludes D&A. In the dominant filer pattern Compustat
removes the FULL DP from COGS, none from SG&A (IBM, INTC, KO, WMT, AAPL, CAT
all show a ~1.00 COGS fraction). 1% -> 57%."}
  {:id :xsga-plus-rd
   :target "XSGA (Compustat)"
   :compustat "XSGA"
   :formula [:+ "SG&A Expense" [:opt "R&D Expense"]]
   :notes "Compustat XSGA folds R&D into SG&A (XRD stays broken out separately as
its own item). 20% -> 42%. Caveat: filers that embed R&D in COGS and tag the
notes value (e.g. HON) are over-added; not detectable from companyfacts."}
  {:id :xsga-components
   :target "XSGA (Compustat)"
   :compustat "XSGA"
   :formula [:+ "Selling and Marketing Expense" "General and Administrative Expense"
             [:opt "R&D Expense"]]
   :notes "Component fallback for filers with no combined SG&A tag (MSFT, ORCL,
CSCO tag S&M and G&A separately)."}
  {:id :gross-profit
   :target "Gross Profit (Compustat)"
   :compustat "REVT - COGS"
   :formula [:- "Revenue" "COGS (Compustat)"]
   :notes "Gross profit under Compustat's COGS definition (i.e. before D&A)."}
  {:id :xopr
   :target "XOPR (Compustat)"
   :compustat "XOPR"
   :formula [:+ "COGS (Compustat)" "XSGA (Compustat)"]
   :notes "Total operating expenses excluding D&A; Compustat's XOPR = COGS + XSGA
identity. 43% within 1%."}
  {:id :special-items
   :target "Special Items (Compustat)"
   :compustat "SPI (operating portion)"
   :formula [:neg-sum "Restructuring Charges" "Impairment Charges" "Goodwill Impairment"
             "Acquisition-Related Costs" "Litigation Settlement"]
   :notes "Compustat treats restructuring and impairment charges as special items
below the operating line. Sign follows Compustat: charges are negative. Only
the operating portion visible in XBRL tags is captured; non-operating special
items (divestiture gains etc.) are not. Double counting is possible when a
filer tags both a combined restructuring-and-impairment concept and a
separate impairment concept."}
  {:id :oiadp
   :target "OIADP (Compustat)"
   :compustat "OIADP"
   :formula [:- "Operating Income" [:opt "Special Items (Compustat)"]]
   :notes "Operating income after depreciation: OperatingIncomeLoss with special-
item charges added back (XBRL operating income includes them; Compustat
excludes them). 24% -> 41%."}
  {:id :oibdp
   :target "OIBDP (Compustat)"
   :compustat "OIBDP"
   :formula [:+ "OIADP (Compustat)" "D&A"]
   :notes "Operating income before depreciation = OIADP + DP. Built top-down from
operating income (28% within 1%) rather than bottom-up as REVT - XOPR (19%);
as a consequence REVT - XOPR (Compustat) and OIBDP (Compustat) need not agree
exactly for firms with expense lines outside the COGS/XSGA reconstruction."}
  {:id :revt-ex-excise
   :target "Revenue (Compustat)"
   :compustat "REVT"
   :formula [:- "Revenue" "Excise Taxes"]
   :guards [[:concept-not-in "Revenue"
             #{"RevenueFromContractWithCustomerExcludingAssessedTax"}]]
   :notes "Compustat REVT is net of excise taxes. Applies only when the winning
revenue concept is not already net of assessed taxes and the filer tags an
excise-tax line. Oil majors may still differ: some (CVX) include equity-
affiliate and other income in their tagged Revenues."}]}
